.TH XD\-SNIP 1 2026-10-22 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-snip \- Snipping Tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-snip
.OP \-\-new\fR[=\fIKIND\fR]
.YS
.SY xd\-snip
.B \-\-copy\-screen
|
.B \-\-copy\-window
|
.B \-\-copy\-stdin
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-snip
is the Windows 7 Snipping Tool, with Windows 10's Delay.
New (or the kind chosen from its arrow) freezes the screen under a white
wash; then
.TP
.B Free-form Snip
draw around what to take; outside the line comes out white.
.TP
.B Rectangular Snip
drag out a rectangle.
.TP
.B Window Snip
click a window (or the desktop, for its monitor).
.TP
.B Full-screen Snip
takes the whole desktop at once.
.PP
Esc cancels.
The snip opens in the Mark-up window, to draw on with a pen (red, blue or
black), the highlighter, or the eraser (which takes away whole strokes),
then Save As (PNG, JPEG or BMP) or Copy.
Options keeps whether snips are copied to the clipboard at once, whether
to ask to save, the white wash, and the selection ink's colour, in
.IR ~/.config/xeondesktop/snip.ini .
.PP
The screen comes from the compositor's wlr-screencopy, where the windows
are from XeonDesktop's xd-window-rectangles-v1 (without it, Window Snip
offers only whole monitors), and the clipboard from ext-data-control:
a copied snip stays on the clipboard after the Snipping Tool closes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-new\fR[=\fIKIND\fR]
Start a snip at once (Win+Shift+S), and quit if it's cancelled.
.I KIND
is
.BR free-form ,
.BR rectangle ,
.B window
or
.BR full-screen ;
without it, the kind last chosen.
.TP
.B \-\-copy\-screen
Copy the whole desktop to the clipboard, without a window (Print Screen).
.TP
.B \-\-copy\-window
Copy the active window to the clipboard (Alt+Print Screen).
.TP
.B \-\-copy\-stdin
Copy a PNG read from standard input to the clipboard.
.PP
The
.B \-\-copy
forms stay running, serving the clipboard, until another program takes it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
.BR xd\-shell (1)
